  "rules": {
    "version": 1,
    "title": "Emberfall Citadel",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How to play",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Choose a hall, then a shot value, and press and hold on the arena to fire, or press Fire. The shot values are 0.04, 0.09, 0.18, 0.36, 0.72, 1.44 and 2.88.",
          "Ember Hall offers 0.04 and 0.09; Ash Hall offers 0.18, 0.36 and 0.72; Inferno Hall offers 1.44 and 2.88. You can change the shot value at any time while you play.",
          "Each ember bolt costs the shot value. Only a bolt that strikes a target is played and charged; a bolt that strikes nothing costs nothing.",
          "When a bolt strikes a target, the server decides whether it is captured. A capture pays the shot value times the target's multiple.",
          "Aim locks the cannon on one target. Auto fire aims at the strongest target in view and stops when you press it again or your balance cannot cover the next shot. Swift shortens the gap between bolts; every bolt is still one shot at your shot value."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "The ember bolt",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The table has one weapon. An ember bolt strikes one target and costs 1x the shot value.",
          "The cannons that appear during a feature show a capture the server has already paid. They are never fired or charged on their own."
        ],
