      {
        "heading": "Features",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A capture of the Hoard Goblin, Soul Lantern Wraith, Rime Wisp, Halo Relic, Ashen Wyrm or Pit Warden plays a feature.",
          "A feature shows the capture's pay in parts. The parts add up to exactly what the capture pays, so a feature never adds to it or takes from it.",
          "A capture of 50x or more shows the Ember banner, 200x or more Blaze, and 500x or more Inferno. The banners do not change the pay."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Return to player",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The published return to player is 96.50 percent of the shot value on every target: a target's capture chance is 0.965 divided by its average multiple, computed exactly on the game's math sheet. Any one session can be higher or lower.",
          "One shot pays at most the lesser of 1,000x the shot value and 2,880.00. At 0.04 that cap is 40.00; at 2.88 it is 2,880.00. The largest multiple on the table is 1,000x, so the cap never cuts a capture short."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Good to know",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The server decides every result before anything moves on screen. What you see is the result it sent, and your balance is the server's balance.",
          "Gold Coins are for promotional play. Sweeps Coins entries and prizes are recorded separately. Both play the same game with the same chances."
        ]
      }
